Name: tabletop-diorama - example (sunny kitchen)
Columns: 4
# One instance of the colour structure in style.md, for a bakery street on a sunny kitchen table.
# Never ship it as is: every game re-chooses each role for its own tone and lighting. demo.html's
# candlelight and morning palettes fill the same roles and pass the same rules.
# Checked with the colour-rules (value = HSV V, chroma = S x V, contrast = WCAG ratio):
#   ink on paper 13.4:1; each signal on paper >= 6.3:1
#   paint chroma 0.19-0.58 (limits 0.15-0.60); paint value 0.48-0.91, spread 0.43
#   wood-bare chroma 0.25, value 0.90; wood-bare on table 2.43:1
#   table chroma 0.30 (paint max 0.58), value 0.64; every paint separates from the table
#   room vs table value 0.21; room chroma 0.13
#   key value 1.00, chroma 0.16; fill chroma 0.16; paper value 0.96, chroma 0.11
#   accent chroma 0.72 vs paint max 0.58; accent hue 60 deg from the table, >= 39 deg from every paint
